{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStoreGuide","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/entitystoreguide"]}],"kind":"article","sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"An ordered, keyed collection with built-in change tracking.","type":"text"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Reference","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/MacrosReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginKillswitchReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginParentalGateReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginPaywallReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginAnalyticsReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginFeatureFlagsReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStoreGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/GettingStarted","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Troubleshooting"],"title":"Reference","generated":true}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore"},{"type":"text","text":" works like a dictionary with insertion-order iteration. Entities must conform to "},{"code":"Identifiable & Equatable & Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" with "},{"code":"UUID","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" as the ID type.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["var cards = EntityStore<Card>()","","cards[card.id] = card                      \/\/ Insert or update — recorded","cards.modify(card.id) { $0.title = \"New\" } \/\/ In-place — recorded only if value changes","cards[card.id] = nil                       \/\/ Delete — recorded","","let card = cards[cardID]                   \/\/ O(1) lookup","let all  = cards.values                    \/\/ Insertion-ordered array","","cards.sort { $0.sortIndex < $1.sortIndex } \/\/ Only marks moved entities","cards.removeAll { $0.isArchived }          \/\/ Rebuilds index in one pass"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every mutation is tracked in a "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ChangeSet","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" that the middleware drains after each reducer call."}]},{"text":"Bulk Deletion","anchor":"Bulk-Deletion","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Each ","type":"text"},{"code":"cards[id] = nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" shifts the storage array’s tail and reindexes the shifted entries — O(tail) per delete, so a loop of k subscript deletes costs O(n·k). To delete many entities at once, use ","type":"text"},{"code":"remove(ids:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (when you have the IDs) or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"removeAll(where:)"},{"type":"text","text":" (when you have a predicate) instead: both remove everything in a single pass with one index rebuild, record the same deletions, and cancel pending upserts exactly like the subscript."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["cards.remove(ids: selection)          \/\/ One pass, not a subscript loop","cards.removeAll { $0.isArchived }"]},{"text":"Merging (Re-hydration)","anchor":"Merging-Re-hydration","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Replacing an "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore"},{"type":"text","text":" after startup destroys any in-memory state that was loaded lazily after initial hydration. Use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"merge(from:shouldReplace:)"},{"type":"text","text":" instead — entities only in the other store are always added, and the closure decides whether an incoming value overwrites the current one:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["\/\/ Absorb DB rows; take an incoming row only when the current one","\/\/ lacks lazily-computed data.","campaigns.merge(from: EntityStore(allFromDB)) { current, incoming in","    current.calculationState == nil && incoming.calculationState != nil","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"merge","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" does not record changes — it has hydration semantics like ","type":"text"},{"code":"init(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"restore(from:)","anchor":"restorefrom"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"restore(from:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" replaces all entities with those from the source store while recording the diff as changes for persistence. Used by undo\/redo (see ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo","type":"reference"},{"text":").","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Deletions"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — IDs in self but absent from source"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Upserts","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — IDs that are new or whose values differ","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Unchanged"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" — identical values produce no change records"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"roleHeading":"Article","title":"EntityStore","role":"article"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/KeyValueStoreGuide":{"title":"KeyValueStore","ident